+# Open questions log — walker-3d-platformer
+
+Recovered by `/gdd reverse --path godot` on 2026-09-27. Every entry below is a `[MISSING]` item from the recovered GDD: the code cannot answer it. Each unanswered question is a production risk until a human decides it.
+
+Format: THE QUESTION / THE STAKES / DECISION DEADLINE / OPTIONS / OWNER / STATUS
+
+| # | Question | Stakes | Deadline | Options | Owner | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| OQ-01 | What is the session goal? There is no win state, no level-complete trigger, no score goal. | Without this, "game" and "demo" mean different things to every team member. Film narration cannot describe what success looks like. | Before film narration is written | (A) Stay demo: document explicitly as "no win state by design." (B) Add win state: collect all 73 coins triggers level-complete. (C) Add win state: eliminate all 4 enemies. | — | Open |
+| OQ-02 | Who is the target player? The GAME-BRIEF says "Walker example." Is the audience a student learning Godot CharacterBody3D, a general game-jam player, or a film viewer? | Determines whether mechanics need polish, whether difficulty needs tuning, and whether narrative matters. | Before v1 | (A) Godot student/learner: inspectability over completeness. (B) Game-jam player: needs win state and challenge. (C) Film viewer: needs readable demonstration of each feature. | — | Open |
+| OQ-03 | What are the design pillars? Nothing in source declares them. | Without pillars, design changes have no rejection criterion. "Can we add a double jump?" has no answer. | Before v2 | (A) Infer from code (Grounded Movement, Readable Camera, Inspectability). (B) Define from scratch as a design exercise. | — | Open |
+| OQ-04 | Can the player be harmed by enemies? Currently no. Enemies patrol and can be shot, but pose no threat to the player. | Removes all tension from the combat system. Shooting enemies is optional busywork without consequences. | Before p1 | (A) By design: enemies are obstacles, not threats. (B) Add contact damage / player health system. | — | Open |
+| OQ-05 | Is the 73-coin collection completable? No total is displayed; no completion event fires. | Player cannot know if they have found every coin. Completion is invisible. | Before p1 | (A) Add coin total to UI: "X / 73". (B) Add collection-complete event. (C) Document as intentional: count is cosmetic. | — | Open |
+| OQ-06 | Is there a narrative? The secret area label ("You have found a secret area!") is the only world text. | Without narrative, the world is geometry and assets. The film has nothing to frame. | Before w2 | (A) No narrative by design. (B) Minimal: add a brief premise (robot exploring ruins). | — | Open |
+| OQ-07 | Should coin collection persist across sessions? Currently session-only; resets on restart. | For a demo, reset is fine. For a game, it signals nothing is earned. | Before p1 | (A) Intentionally session-only (document). (B) Add save/load via ConfigFile or JSON. | — | Open |
+| OQ-08 | Is there background music? No music node or resource observed in any script or scene. | SFX-only creates a sparse audio atmosphere; acceptable for a demo, thin for a game. | Before p3 | (A) No music by design. (B) Add looping background track. | — | Open |
+| OQ-09 | Are the 7 Texture RID shutdown leaks acceptable? Reported on every run; not suppressed. | Not a gameplay risk, but signals incomplete resource cleanup. Could mask genuine leaks later. | Before production | (A) Investigate and fix. (B) Document as known Godot 4.7 import artifact. | — | Open |
+| OQ-10 | Is touch hardware ever tested on a real device? Joystick verified synthetically only. | Touch controls are unproven. The film cannot claim mobile support. | Before film | (A) Verify on physical device. (B) Label explicitly as "synthetic test only, hardware unverified." | — | Open |
diff --git a/godot/checkpoint/checkpoint_pad.gd b/godot/checkpoint/checkpoint_pad.gd
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e65b35b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/godot/checkpoint/checkpoint_pad.gd
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+class_name CheckpointPad
+extends Area3D
+
+var activation_count: int = 0
+var respawn_point: Vector3 = Vector3.ZERO
+
+func _ready() -> void:
+	body_entered.connect(_on_body_entered)
+
+func _on_body_entered(body: Node3D) -> void:
+	if activation_count > 0:
+		return
+	if not body is Player:
+		return
+	activation_count += 1
+	# Snap XZ to pad centre; use player's Y (floor level when walking in)
+	respawn_point = Vector3(global_position.x, body.global_position.y, global_position.z)
+	body.respawn_point = respawn_point
